1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:16,000
One doodle, one project, one visible timeline shared by a human and an agent.

2
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:38,000
The browser reads the real pixels locally. No paid vision model is required.

3
00:00:38,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Native WebMCP discovers ten structured creative tools directly from the page.

4
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:32,000
The agent changes the mood and rewrites a shot. The same UI changes immediately.

5
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:56,000
Reordering shots rebuilds a coherent zero-to-fifteen-second timeline.

6
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:16,000
The exact project survives save and reload, so the human can continue without copying state.

7
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:32,000
Without a verified renderer, the project stops truthfully at prompt-ready.

8
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:40,000
You are me, I am you: two collaborators shaping one visible artifact.
